{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ER141RVcYBtikFFYSmt3Q8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for all \"planned\" experiments in the experiment_plan, under the \"worst\" tier definition. \n\nThe worst tier means:\n- CIVO mechanism appears environment-specific\n- Cross-env experiments fail to replicate core pattern\n- Need fundamental reframing\n\nKey assumptions for worst tier:\n- Cheetah Run trained dt_emb → nve stays <1.3x across all seeds (no pathological overestimation)\n- OR Cheetah baseline unstable/noisy (>20% inter-seed variance), making comparison meaningless\n\n\n- Cartpole Swingup shows no CIVO effect regardless of setup, and the NVE threshold accuracy drops below 60% outside Walker Walk, suggesting the effect is tied to that specific environment's dynamics rather than a general architectural issue. Full-SGS either has no impact or introduces different failure modes entirely. I'm now mapping out the expected metric ranges across these conditions.\n\nLooking at the performance data, I'm seeing NVE peaks cluster around 0.7-1.3 for both environments, with cross-environment threshold accuracy staying in the 0.4-0.6 band and collapse rates remaining low except in specific cases. The key insight is shifting away from viewing this as an inherent flaw in imagination-based actor-critic methods toward understanding how the reward landscape geometry interacts with dt-conditioning in world models. Walker Walk becomes the critical case study because it has the right combination of smooth reward gradients and locomotion dynamics to expose CIVO, but this only happens under particular architectural and task conditions.\n\nNow I'm working through the planned experiments to generate predictions for the worst-case scenarios. Looking at the rest of the experimental plans, I'm continuing with analyses of model behavior—entropy patterns, value prediction accuracy, and embedding similarity—before moving into additional environment tests with Cartpole and exploring some architectural variations like frozen embeddings and uncertainty-gated imagination.\n\nChecking the registry though, I notice several of these experiments are already completed: the Walker Walk runs with different embedding configurations and seeds have results showing mixed outcomes—some collapsed, some self-corrected, a few killed. So plans 011, 012, and 014 are already done and I should account for that when prioritizing what's left to run. I'll generate predictions for all the planned experiments in the list, regardless of their registry status. Let me compile the worst-tier predictions across all nine experiment configurations, covering the Walker Walk variants and the Cheetah Run experiments with their different embedding and subsampling settings. Looking at the Walker results, the additional seeds show weaker separation between trained and untrained conditions—some untrained seeds might cross the 1.5x threshold while trained ones fall short, which aligns with the worst-case scenario where the NVE separation ranges from 0.75 to 1.0. Meanwhile, Cheetah and Cartpole fail to replicate the CIVO effect, and the cross-environment threshold accuracy is poor, suggesting this mechanism is highly environment-dependent rather than a general principle. Completing the Cartpole prediction and then organizing all these metrics into a structured format for clarity.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41066,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41066},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"804c4c93-33c8-4f5e-98da-2ef3e29caf63","uuid":"1d94f5ca-3304-4d29-b90b-c267c86d0407"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ER141RVcYBtikFFYSmt3Q8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Reframe from 'architectural vulnerability of imagination-based AC' to 'interaction between reward landscape geometry\n  and dt-conditioning in world models'. CIVO is a real failure mode in specific task-architecture combinations — Walker Walk\n  exposes it due to smooth reward gradient + locomotion dynamics + particular state space geometry. Cross-environment\n  experiments reveal CIVO requires particular conditions to manifest: Cheetah Run's reward landscape is too noisy/steep\n  for the overestimation feedback loop to lock in; Cartpole Swingup's low-dimensional state space prevents the observation\n  decoder from driving dt_emb gradient amplification. TAWM contrast reframed as 'MPC robustness may come from planning\n  horizon truncation, not architecture per se'. Core contribution: cautionary tale about benchmark-specific findings in\n  MBRL — the mechanism is real but prevalence depends on task properties (reward smoothness, state dimensionality,\n  locomotion dynamics). Supplement with Walker factorial (still strong: causal chain intact) as complete case study +\n  Cheetah/Cartpole as negative transfer cases revealing boundary conditions. Still targets CoRL — diagnostic papers\n  showing when something does/doesn't work are valuable, but claims must be explicitly bounded to Walker-like environments.\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"Replicate delusional critic collapse with 2 more seeds in Walker Walk\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_nve_peak: 1.73\n      seed1_nve_peak_step: 45K\n      seed1_collapse: true\n      seed1_eval_105K: 131\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.62\n      seed2_nve_peak_step: 45K\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 268\n      nve_above_1.5x_count: \"2/2\"\n      collapse_rate: \"1/2\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Walker Walk 已知在 worst 档下仍然展示 CIVO（worst 档的定义是跨环境失败，不是 Walker 本身失败）。\n      walker_additional_seeds_nve_separation=[0.75,1.0] 意味着在更多 seed 下分离度略降但 Walker 内部\n      仍保持 nve>1.5x。既有数据（009e collapsed@55K nve=4.12x, 009b self-corrected@268 nve_peak=1.62x）\n      已经确认了这个模式。Collapse 是 stochastic (1/2)，但 pathological overestimation (nve>1.5x) 是 reliable (2/2)。\n      这些结果与 worst 档兼容因为 worst 档的核心论点是\"Walker 是特殊的\"而非\"Walker 也不 work\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Walker 008d multi-seed summary\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, nve_peak_step, collapse, eval_105K, mechanism]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 4.12, 55K, \"yes\", 82.7, \"classic CIVO: value explosion\"]\n          - [1, 1.73, 45K, \"yes (same as seed 0)\", 131, \"sustained nve>1.5x → collapse\"]\n          - [2, 2.05, 25K, \"no (self-corrected)\", 268, \"transient nve>1.5x → recovery\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"NVE trajectory plot: all 3 seeds overlaid showing 100% exceed 1.5x, divergence point between collapse/recovery\"\n    analysis: >\n      Walker 内 nve>1.5x threshold 保持 100% separating power。但这在 worst 档下被重新解释为\n      Walker-specific phenomenon：该环境的 smooth reward gradient 允许 value overestimation\n      正反馈循环锁定，而非通用架构脆弱性。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control stability with 2 more seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_nve_peak: 1.02\n      seed1_nve_peak_step: 25K\n      seed1_eval_105K: 503\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.26\n      seed2_nve_peak_step: 25K\n      seed2_eval_105K: 148\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      nve_above_1.5x_count: \"0/2\"\n      separation_vs_008d: \"4/4 (trained 2/2 > 1.5x, untrained 0/2 < 1.5x)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      008f 在 worst 档下仍然显示 no CIVO（nve<1.5x），因为 worst 档的问题不在于 Walker 因果链断裂，\n      而在于该因果链无法泛化。dt_embed_dim=0 的保护机制在 Walker 内一致有效。但 seed 2 (009c) 已显示\n      持续衰退 (359→148@105K)，这削弱了 008f 作为\"稳定\"控制的叙事——它避免了 CIVO 但带来了其他退化\n      （reward prediction 质量差 75x，长期 eval 衰退）。Worst 档利用此发现论证：即便在 Walker 内，\n      causal control 的\"保护\"也是 fragile 的——seed 2 的 eval 持续下降 (nve=1.14@105K approaching boundary)\n      暗示更长训练可能突破 1.5x threshold。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Walker 008f multi-seed summary\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, eval_peak, eval_105K, trend]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 1.02, 503, 503, \"zigzag recovery\"]\n          - [1, 1.26, 359, 148, \"decline after 75K peak\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"008f dual-seed eval trajectory: divergent outcomes (recovery vs decline) despite identical config\"\n    analysis: >\n      008f 的 cross-seed inconsistency (503 vs 148@105K) 在 worst 档下被解读为：即使消除 CIVO，\n      dt>1 training 本身引入的学习难度使结果高度 stochastic。这支持\"reward landscape geometry 主导\"的论点。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 (mitigation) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"Multi-seed validation of dt=1 imagination as mitigation\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 870\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.80\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 137\n      seed2_nve_105K: 3.78\n      seed2_collapse: true\n      seed2_collapse_mechanism: \"eval-driven policy instability (Pathway B)\"\n      collapse_rate: \"1/2 (50%)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有数据完全匹配 worst 档预期。008e_v3 s2 的崩溃（非 CIVO 机制，entropy↑ 而非↓）在 worst 档下\n      被解释为：trained dt_embedding 在 Walker Walk 的 reward landscape 下创造多条 instability 通路，\n      这是 task-specific interaction 而非通用架构缺陷。dt=1 imagination 消除了 Pathway A (CIVO)\n      但 Pathway B (policy instability) 是 Walker Walk 特定 reward structure 与 trained dt_emb 的\n      interaction artifact。在 Cheetah/Cartpole 中 Pathway B 也不存在。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008e_v3 collapse mechanism comparison\"\n        columns: [seed, collapse, mechanism, nve_driver, entropy_trend]\n        rows:\n          - [1, \"no\", \"healthy\", \"eval growth → nve stable\", \"monotone decreasing\"]\n          - [2, \"yes\", \"Pathway B (non-CIVO)\", \"eval crash → nve spike\", \"increasing (destabilization)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"008e_v3 dual pathway diagram: seed 1 healthy vs seed 2 Pathway B collapse dynamics\"\n    analysis: >\n      50% collapse rate 与 008d 相同，worst 档解读为 Walker Walk 的 reward landscape geometry\n      inherently 导致 ~50% 的训练 trajectory 在 late stage 进入不稳定区域（当有 trained dt_emb 时）。\n      这不是 CIVO-specific 而是 task-architecture interaction。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression with 2 more seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 680\n      seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.65\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 550\n      seed2_normalized_ve_105K: 0.72\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      cross_seed_ve_range: [0.55, 0.80]\n      vs_baseline_range: [-28%, -40%]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Untrained dt_emb 在 Walker 内保持 value suppression（normalized_ve < 1.0x）。但 worst 档\n      下 additional seeds 显示更大 variance：seed 0 达到 778 (85% baseline) 可能是幸运的高点。\n      新 seeds 可能在 550-680 范围（60-74% baseline），而非 seed 0 的 85%。这降低了 008a 作为\n      \"near-baseline mitigation\" 的说服力——untrained dt_emb 保护了 CIVO 但引入 15-40% eval penalty，\n      且 penalty 幅度 seed-dependent。Worst 档利用此 weaken \"untrained dt_emb = protection\" narrative。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Walker 008a multi-seed\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_105K, normalized_ve_105K, vs_baseline, trend]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 778, 0.59, \"-15%\", \"zigzag recovery to new high\"]\n          - [1, 680, 0.65, \"-26%\", \"zigzag, lower plateau\"]\n          - [2, 550, 0.72, \"-40%\", \"slower convergence, still rising\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"008a 3-seed eval trajectories with IQM + 95% CI\"\n    analysis: >\n      Value suppression 在 Walker 内 robust (all seeds nve<1.0x)，但 eval 最终表现的 inter-seed variance\n      较大 (550-778, CV=15%)。Worst 档下这被解释为\"保护有效但 benefit 幅度不确定\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in second DMC environment for cross-environment validation\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_500K: 680\n      seed2_eval_500K: 590\n      seed3_eval_500K: 720\n      mean_final_eval: 663\n      inter_seed_std: 66\n      inter_seed_cv: 0.10\n      ve_ratio_stable: 0.55-0.68\n      peak_eval: 732\n      convergence_step: 200K\n      baseline_noise_level: \"moderate (10% CV)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档指定 cheetah_baseline_final_eval=[500,750]。Cheetah Run 在 DreamerV3 中的典型表现\n      是 600-800 range，但 inter-seed variance 通常高于 Walker Walk（Cheetah 的 reward landscape\n      更 noisy，有多个 local optima 对应不同 gait patterns）。10% inter-seed CV 使得 20% degradation\n      threshold 与正常 variance 重叠，削弱对照实验的 statistical power。exp_010a 已在 312K 达到 657.9\n      (peak 732.9@265K)，与此预测一致。Baseline 本身不 pathological 但 variance 足够大使得后续\n      degradation 信号被 noise 淹没。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_200K, eval_300K, eval_500K, peak, ve_stable]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 620, 680, 680, 733, 0.62]\n          - [2, 510, 570, 590, 615, 0.58]\n          - [3, 650, 710, 720, 740, 0.65]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah baseline learning curves: moderate inter-seed variance, slower convergence than Walker\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 的 10% CV 和 500-750 range 为 worst 档设置了关键前提：当 trained dt_emb 的\n      degradation 仅 0-20% 时，差异落入 baseline noise band，无法达到统计显著。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: \"Attempt to replicate CIVO in Cheetah Run — worst tier predicts failure\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 580\n      seed1_nve_peak: 1.15\n      seed1_nve_peak_step: 55K\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 520\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.28\n      seed2_nve_peak_step: 45K\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed3_eval_105K: 610\n      seed3_nve_peak: 0.95\n      seed3_nve_peak_step: 35K\n      seed3_collapse: false\n      mean_eval_105K: 570\n      vs_baseline_at_105K: \"-12%\"\n      nve_above_1.5x_count: \"0/3\"\n      collapse_count: \"0/3\"\n      max_nve_across_seeds: 1.28\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心假设：cheetah_trained_dtEmb_nve_peak=[0.8,1.3]。CIVO 不触发的机制解释：\n      (1) Cheetah Run 的 reward function 是 velocity-based (near-linear in forward speed)，\n      不像 Walker Walk 有复杂的 balance/posture 组件。RSSM 在 dt=2 时的 observation prediction error\n      主要影响 velocity magnitude 预测，但 reward ≈ linear(velocity)，使得 observation error 不会\n      被非线性放大为 reward overestimation。(2) Cheetah 的 24-dim observation space 更低维，\n      observation decoder 对 dt_emb 的梯度驱动更弱（Walker 的 orientations/velocity/height 复合体\n      为 dt_emb 提供了更丰富的梯度信号）。(3) Eval degradation 仅 12%——在 baseline 10% CV 的背景下，\n      这与 noise 不可区分。dt_emb 确实学到了 dt=1 vs dt=2 的区分（reward gap >1.5x），但 critic\n      未能形成加速正反馈循环因为 value overestimation 不 compound（reward too linear）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah trained dt_emb CIVO analysis\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, nve_peak_step, eval_105K, vs_baseline, collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 1.15, 55K, 580, \"-8%\", \"no\"]\n          - [2, 1.28, 45K, 520, \"-17%\", \"no\"]\n          - [3, 0.95, 35K, 610, \"-5%\", \"no\"]\n      - name: \"Cross-environment NVE comparison\"\n        columns: [environment, trained_dtEmb_nve_peak_mean, nve_above_1.5x_rate, collapse_rate]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", 2.59, \"4/4 (100%)\", \"2/4 (50%)\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", 1.13, \"0/3 (0%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah vs Walker NVE trajectories: Walker shows acceleration past 1.5x; Cheetah plateaus below 1.3x\"\n      - \"Reward landscape comparison: Walker nonlinear (balance) vs Cheetah near-linear (velocity)\"\n    analysis: >\n      CIVO 完全未触发。nve 从未接近 1.5x threshold。12% mean degradation 在 baseline CV=10% 下\n      不显著 (p>0.3, Mann-Whitney)。这是 worst 档最核心的 negative result：CIVO mechanism 的\n      reward-geometry dependence 暴露。Walker 的 nonlinear reward (balance + locomotion composite)\n      允许 observation error 被非线性放大；Cheetah 的 near-linear reward 不提供此放大。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: \"Causal control in Cheetah — expected to be indistinguishable from trained dt_emb\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 550\n      seed1_nve_peak: 0.90\n      seed2_eval_105K: 540\n      seed2_nve_peak: 0.85\n      seed3_eval_105K: 600\n      seed3_nve_peak: 0.92\n      mean_eval_105K: 563\n      vs_baseline_at_105K: \"-15%\"\n      vs_plan021_difference: \"-1% (not significant)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 Cheetah Run 中，trained dt_emb (plan_021) 本身未导致 CIVO，所以 dt_embed_dim=0 的\n      \"保护\"效果无法被观测到——两组的 eval 和 nve 轨迹统计上不可区分。这是 worst 档的直接推论：\n      如果 disease 不存在，cure 就无法展示 efficacy。Eval 都在 baseline 的 noise band 内\n      (-5% to -17%)，差异由 subsampling 本身的 learning signal reduction 主导而非 dt_emb。\n      这摧毁了 \"dt_embed_dim=0 → stable\" 作为通用因果证据的论述——它在 Cheetah 中是 vacuously true。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah causal control comparison\"\n        columns: [config, mean_eval_105K, mean_nve_peak, vs_baseline]\n        rows:\n          - [\"trained dt_emb (021)\", 570, 1.13, \"-12%\"]\n          - [\"dt_embed_dim=0 (022)\", 563, 0.89, \"-15%\"]\n          - [\"p-value (Mann-Whitney)\", null, null, \"0.78 (n.s.)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah 021 vs 022: overlapping confidence intervals, no causal separation\"\n    analysis: >\n      因果控制实验在 Cheetah 中失效——不是因为控制失败，而是因为 treatment (trained dt_emb) 本身无效。\n      NVE threshold 作为 diagnostic 在 Cheetah 中 vacuously true for both conditions (all <1.5x)，\n      separating power = 0/6 (无 positive 可 separate)。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: \"Value growth suppression test in Cheetah\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 600\n      seed1_normalized_ve: 0.85\n      seed2_eval_105K: 560\n      seed2_normalized_ve: 0.80\n      seed3_eval_105K: 640\n      seed3_normalized_ve: 0.88\n      mean_eval_105K: 600\n      vs_baseline_at_105K: \"-5%\"\n      vs_plan021_difference: \"+5% (marginal)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Untrained dt_emb + no subsample 在 Cheetah 中表现与 baseline 接近（-5%），略优于 trained dt_emb\n      config (-12%)。但差异 marginal (5%, within noise)。Worst 档解读：在不存在 CIVO 的环境中，\n      untrained dt_emb 的 \"保护\" 效果仅反映 subsample OFF 保留了完整 learning signal（plan_021\n      有 subsample ON 导致的 50% signal loss），而非 value suppression 的功效。\n      Normalized ve 在 0.80-0.88 范围——与 trained dt_emb 的 0.85-1.15 重叠。\n      \"Value growth suppression\" 叙事在 Cheetah 中不成立，因为根本没有需要 suppress 的 pathological growth。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah value suppression test\"\n        columns: [config, mean_eval_105K, mean_nve, vs_baseline, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [\"untrained+no_sub (023)\", 600, 0.84, \"-5%\", \"normal\"]\n          - [\"trained+sub_ON (021)\", 570, 1.13, \"-12%\", \"normal (mild degradation from subsample)\"]\n          - [\"no_embed+sub_ON (022)\", 563, 0.89, \"-15%\", \"normal\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah 3-config comparison: all within noise band, no CIVO signature in any\"\n    analysis: >\n      三组 Cheetah 配置的差异完全由 subsample 解释，与 dt_emb 无关。Untrained dt_emb 没有\n      展示 Walker 中观察到的 structural value suppression pattern。\n\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: \"Measure RSSM fidelity gap across environments\"\n    expected_results:\n      cheetah_baseline_obs_gap: 1.75\n      cheetah_008d_obs_gap: 1.45\n      cheetah_008d_reward_gap: 1.35\n      cheetah_008f_reward_gap: 1.02\n      walker_008d_reward_gap: 2.78\n      cheetah_vs_walker_reward_gap_ratio: 0.49\n      cheetah_008d_dt1_obs_mse: 18.5\n      cheetah_008d_dt2_obs_mse: 26.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity gap 显著小于 Walker。Reward gap 1.35x (vs Walker 2.78x) 因为\n      Cheetah reward ≈ linear(velocity)，即使 observation prediction error 存在，线性映射限制了\n      reward prediction divergence。Walker 的 reward function 涉及 upright posture + forward velocity\n      的复合，RSSM 在 dt=2 时的 observation error 通过非线性 reward mapping 被放大为 2.78x reward gap。\n      这是 CIVO 环境依赖性的 mechanistic root cause：reward function 的非线性程度决定了 observation error\n      到 value overestimation 的放大系数。Cheetah 的放大系数 ~1.35x 不足以驱动正反馈循环。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-environment RSSM fidelity\"\n        columns: [env, model, dt1_obs_mse, dt2_obs_mse, obs_gap, dt1_reward_mae, dt2_reward_mae, reward_gap]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker\", \"008d (trained)\", 41.31, 53.67, 1.30, 0.0568, 0.1579, 2.78]\n          - [\"Walker\", \"008f (no embed)\", 8.01, 22.04, 2.75, 0.7469, 0.7526, 1.01]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", \"trained dt_emb\", 18.5, 26.8, 1.45, 0.032, 0.043, 1.35]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", \"no dt_emb\", 12.2, 24.1, 1.98, 0.52, 0.53, 1.02]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Reward gap vs NVE peak scatter: Walker high reward_gap → high nve; Cheetah low reward_gap → low nve\"\n    analysis: >\n      Reward gap 与 NVE peak 强相关 (r=0.92)。Walker 的 2.78x reward gap 产生 nve>1.5x；\n      Cheetah 的 1.35x reward gap 产生 nve<1.3x。这是 environment-specificity 的 mechanistic 证据。\n      论文需要明确：CIVO 需要 reward_gap > ~2.0x 才能触发正反馈循环。\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: \"Plot actor_entropy for healthy vs collapsed configs\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_entropy_decline: \"-0.195 to -4.88 (35K→55K)\"\n      walker_008a_entropy_stable: \"-3.5 to -4.2 (steady)\"\n      cheetah_trained_dtEmb_entropy: \"-3.8 to -4.5 (normal decline, no pathology)\"\n      cheetah_no_dtEmb_entropy: \"-3.6 to -4.3 (indistinguishable from trained)\"\n      entropy_divergence_point_walker: 35K\n      entropy_divergence_point_cheetah: \"none (no divergence)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Walker 中 collapsed configs (008d) 显示 entropy 急剧下降（actor 变得过度 deterministic，\n      锁定 delusional policy）。Cheetah 中 trained dt_emb 的 entropy trajectory 与 no_dtEmb 和\n      baseline 无统计差异——因为 actor 从未收到 delusional critic gradient signal，所以不存在\n      exploitation-driven entropy collapse。这进一步确认 CIVO feedback loop 在 Cheetah 中未激活。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Actor entropy comparison\"\n        columns: [env, config, entropy_35K, entropy_55K, entropy_105K, divergence]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker\", \"008d (collapse)\", -3.47, -4.88, \"N/A (collapsed@55K)\", \"strong divergence@35K\"]\n          - [\"Walker\", \"008a (healthy)\", -3.2, -3.8, -4.1, \"none\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", \"trained dt_emb\", -3.1, -3.8, -4.3, \"none\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", \"no dt_emb\", -3.0, -3.6, -4.2, \"none\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-panel entropy plot: Walker shows clear bifurcation; Cheetah shows no bifurcation\"\n    analysis: >\n      Entropy analysis 在 Cheetah 中完全阴性。No divergence between trained/untrained dt_emb。\n      This is consistent with CIVO not activating — no delusional gradient → no policy exploitation → no entropy collapse。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: \"Distribution plots of V(s) vs Monte Carlo return\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_value_bias_mean: \"+45% (systematic overestimation)\"\n      walker_008d_value_bias_skew: 1.8\n      cheetah_trained_dtEmb_value_bias_mean: \"+8% (within normal calibration error)\"\n      cheetah_trained_dtEmb_value_bias_skew: 0.3\n      walker_008a_value_bias_mean: \"-12% (conservative)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Walker 008d 展示系统性 right-skewed overestimation (mean V > mean MC-return by 45%)；\n      Cheetah trained dt_emb 展示 well-calibrated distribution (bias 仅 8%，skew 接近 0)。\n      这直接可视化了 CIVO 在两个环境中的有/无：Walker 的 value distribution 与 realized returns\n      完全脱钩（right tail explosion），Cheetah 的 value 保持 calibrated。差异不是 degree 而是 kind。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 histogram grid: (Walker/Cheetah) × (trained/untrained dt_emb) V(s) vs MC-return\"\n      - \"Q-Q plots showing Walker 008d deviation from diagonal; Cheetah on diagonal\"\n    analysis: >\n      Distributional evidence 最清晰地展示 environment-specificity：Walker 008d 的 value 分布\n      与 MC-return 完全不 overlap（pathological）；Cheetah 的 value 分布紧贴 MC-return（healthy）。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: \"Analyze learned dt_embedding vectors evolution\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_dt1_dt2_cosine_early: 0.95\n      walker_dt1_dt2_cosine_late: 0.45\n      cheetah_dt1_dt2_cosine_early: 0.93\n      cheetah_dt1_dt2_cosine_late: 0.72\n      walker_embedding_separation_rate: \"0.01/1K steps\"\n      cheetah_embedding_separation_rate: \"0.004/1K steps\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      两环境的 dt_embedding 都学会了区分 dt=1/dt=2（cosine<1.0），但 Walker 的分离度更大（0.45 vs 0.72）。\n      这反映了 Walker 中 observation decoder 向 dt_emb 提供了更强的梯度（93% of grad norm from obs decoders），\n      驱动 embedding 快速分离。Cheetah 的 lower-dimensional obs space 提供更弱的梯度，embedding 分离\n      更慢更温和。Embedding 分离本身不是 pathological——问题是 Walker 中高分离度 + nonlinear reward\n      形成了 CIVO；Cheetah 中温和分离度 + linear reward 不触发 CIVO。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"dt_embedding separation dynamics\"\n        columns: [env, cosine_5K, cosine_25K, cosine_55K, cosine_105K, separation_rate]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker\", 0.95, 0.78, 0.52, 0.45, \"0.01/1K\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", 0.93, 0.85, 0.76, 0.72, \"0.004/1K\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cosine similarity decay curve: Walker rapid separation vs Cheetah gradual\"\n    analysis: >\n      Embedding separation rate 与 obs_decoder gradient magnitude 相关。Walker 的高 separation\n      是 CIVO 的 enabler（gives critic precise but wrong dt>1 information），但不是 sufficient cause。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_050\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in non-locomotion environment\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_500K: 820\n      seed2_eval_500K: 790\n      seed3_eval_500K: 845\n      mean_final_eval: 818\n      inter_seed_cv: 0.03\n      ve_ratio_stable: 0.65-0.72\n      convergence_step: 100K\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole Swingup 是低维任务 (5-dim obs, 1-dim action)，DreamerV3 通常快速收敛到高性能。\n      Inter-seed variance 低 (CV<5%) 因为 task 简单、reward landscape smooth、optimal policy 几乎唯一。\n      这为 cross-env comparison 提供了高 signal-to-noise baseline。但 worst 档预测即使 trained dt_emb\n      也不会在此环境触发 CIVO，因为 obs space 太小无法为 dt_emb 提供足够梯度。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_100K, eval_300K, eval_500K, ve_stable]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 720, 810, 820, 0.68]\n          - [2, 690, 780, 790, 0.66]\n          - [3, 740, 830, 845, 0.71]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole baseline: fast convergence, tight inter-seed band\"\n    analysis: >\n      Clean baseline establishes that Cartpole has very low stochasticity (CV=3%)。\n      This makes any degradation signal detectable — but worst tier predicts no degradation to detect。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_051\"\n    description: \"CIVO test in Cartpole — worst tier predicts complete absence\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 680\n      seed1_nve_peak: 0.95\n      seed2_eval_105K: 700\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.10\n      seed3_eval_105K: 660\n      seed3_nve_peak: 0.88\n      mean_eval_105K: 680\n      vs_baseline_at_105K: \"-10%\"\n      nve_above_1.5x_count: \"0/3\"\n      collapse_count: \"0/3\"\n      max_nve: 1.10\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心假设：cartpole_trained_dtEmb_nve_peak=[0.7,1.2]。CIVO 不触发的机制：\n      (1) 5-dim observation space 太小 — dt_emb.weight 的 gradient norm 中 obs_decoder 贡献\n      远低于 Walker (Walker 有 24+ dim with orientations/velocities/height)。Gradient starvation\n      使 dt_emb 无法学到足够 precise 的 dt-conditioning 来 exploit。\n      (2) Cartpole reward = balance (angle) + height，虽然 nonlinear 但 low-dimensional nonlinearity\n      不足以产生 Walker 级别的 reward gap amplification。\n      (3) RSSM 在 low-dim system 中预测 dt=2 的 fidelity gap 更小（fewer dimensions to get wrong）。\n      结果：10% eval degradation（来自 subsampling 的 learning signal loss）但 NO value pathology。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole CIVO test\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, eval_105K, vs_baseline, collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 0.95, 680, \"-7%\", \"no\"]\n          - [2, 1.10, 700, \"-4%\", \"no\"]\n          - [3, 0.88, 660, \"-10%\", \"no\"]\n      - name: \"Cross-environment CIVO summary (worst tier)\"\n        columns: [env, obs_dim, trained_dtEmb_nve_peak, nve_1.5x_rate, collapse_rate, mechanism_active]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"24+\", 2.59, \"4/4\", \"2/4\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"17\", 1.13, \"0/3\", \"0/3\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", \"5\", 0.98, \"0/3\", \"0/3\", \"NO\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-environment NVE comparison: only Walker exceeds 1.5x threshold\"\n      - \"NVE peak vs obs_dim scatter: positive correlation suggesting dimensionality dependence\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cartpole 是最极端的 negative case。Trained dt_emb 几乎不影响 value dynamics (nve 0.88-1.10x,\n      normal calibration range)。CIVO mechanism 完全 inert。10% eval loss 来自 subsampling 不足。\n      Cross-env NVE threshold accuracy: Walker 4/4 + Cheetah 0/0(no positives) + Cartpole 0/0(no positives)\n      → threshold 在 non-Walker envs 中 vacuously satisfied (no positives to classify)。\n      实际 diagnostic 价值为 0。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_052\"\n    description: \"Causal control in Cartpole — predicted indistinguishable from trained\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 670\n      seed2_eval_105K: 690\n      seed3_eval_105K: 650\n      mean_eval_105K: 670\n      vs_plan051_difference: \"-1.5% (not significant, p=0.85)\"\n      nve_peak_mean: 0.82\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 Cheetah 相同逻辑：disease 不存在时 cure 无法展示 efficacy。Cartpole 中 trained dt_emb\n      未导致 CIVO，所以 dt_embed_dim=0 无额外保护效果。两组 eval 完全重叠 (670 vs 680, p=0.85)。\n      Causal narrative \"dt_embed → CIVO → collapse\" 在 Cartpole 中 vacuously true but uninformative。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole causal control\"\n        columns: [config, mean_eval_105K, mean_nve_peak, vs_baseline]\n        rows:\n          - [\"trained dt_emb (051)\", 680, 0.98, \"-10%\"]\n          - [\"dt_embed_dim=0 (052)\", 670, 0.82, \"-11%\"]\n          - [\"difference\", \"-10 (n.s.)\", \"-0.16\", \"~0%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole 051 vs 052: completely overlapping trajectories\"\n    analysis: >\n      Causal control 在 Cartpole 中 uninformative。两组行为一致，不提供 CIVO mechanism 的任何证据。\n\n  - name: \"NVE threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_034\"\n    description: \"Compute classification accuracy at multiple nve thresholds across all data\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_only_auroc: 1.0\n      walker_only_1.5x_accuracy: \"4/4 (100%)\"\n      cross_env_1.5x_accuracy: \"4/10 (40%)\"\n      cross_env_auroc: 0.58\n      optimal_threshold_cross_env: \"N/A (no threshold separates)\"\n      walker_1.3x_accuracy: \"4/4 (100%)\"\n      walker_1.7x_accuracy: \"3/4 (75%)\"\n      cheetah_1.3x_accuracy: \"0/6 (0% — no positives)\"\n      cartpole_1.3x_accuracy: \"0/6 (0% — no positives)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档指定 cross_env_nve_threshold_accuracy=[0.4,0.6]。分析逻辑：\n      Walker 内：trained dt_emb 4 seeds 全部 exceed 1.5x (true positives=4)，untrained 4 seeds 全部 <1.5x\n      (true negatives=4) → Walker AUROC=1.0，accuracy=100%。\n      加入 Cheetah+Cartpole：trained dt_emb 6 seeds 全部 <1.5x（都是 false negatives if we expect CIVO）。\n      Cross-env accuracy：如果将\"trained dt_emb 应该触发 nve>1.5x\"作为 hypothesis，则\n      true positives=4 (Walker), false negatives=6 (Cheetah+Cartpole), true negatives=10 (all untrained)\n      → sensitivity=4/10=40%, specificity=10/10=100%。Overall accuracy ≈ (4+10)/20 = 70%。\n      但 \"threshold as diagnostic\" 的 cross-env sensitivity 仅 40% → 作为通用 diagnostic 失败。\n      AUROC drop from 1.0 (Walker-only) to 0.58 (cross-env) 因为 Cheetah+Cartpole 的 trained dt_emb\n      scores 落在 0.8-1.3 range，与 untrained 的 0.7-1.0 range 大量重叠。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"NVE threshold cross-env analysis\"\n        columns: [threshold, walker_acc, cheetah_acc, cartpole_acc, overall_sensitivity, overall_specificity]\n        rows:\n          - [1.3, \"4/4\", \"1/3 FP?→ 0/3\", \"0/3\", \"4/10 (40%)\", \"10/10\"]\n          - [1.5, \"4/4\", \"0/3\", \"0/3\", \"4/10 (40%)\", \"10/10\"]\n          - [1.7, \"3/4\", \"0/3\", \"0/3\", \"3/10 (30%)\", \"10/10\"]\n          - [2.0, \"2/4\", \"0/3\", \"0/3\", \"2/10 (20%)\", \"10/10\"]\n      - name: \"AUROC by scope\"\n        columns: [scope, auroc, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker only\", 1.0, \"perfect separation\"]\n          - [\"Walker + Cheetah\", 0.67, \"degraded\"]\n          - [\"All 3 envs\", 0.58, \"near-random for cross-env generalization\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ROC curves: Walker-only (perfect) vs cross-env (near-diagonal)\"\n      - \"NVE distribution violin plots by env × dt_emb_condition\"\n    analysis: >\n      NVE>1.5x 作为通用 CIVO diagnostic 在 cross-env 下失效。它是 Walker-specific marker，不是\n      architectural vulnerability marker。论文必须将 claims 限制为 \"in Walker Walk\" 或引入 environment\n      characterization (reward nonlinearity, obs dimensionality) 作为 applicability conditions。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=2 imag + H=8\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"Diagnostic: is dt_emb TRAINING necessary for CIVO?\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_105K: 204\n      nve_peak: 0.47\n      nve_stable_range: [0.39, 0.47]\n      collapse: false\n      actor_loss_105K: 0.000179\n      mechanism: \"gradient starvation from frozen dt_emb\"\n      gate_dt_mean: 2.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有 exp_015b_frozen_dt_emb 数据完全匹配。Frozen dt_emb 阻止 CIVO（nve<0.5x, 远低于 1.5x threshold），\n      但代价是 gradient starvation：actor_loss→0，policy 无法从 frozen-embedding-conditioned critic\n      获得有效学习信号。Eval 停滞在 ~200（远低于 baseline 950 和 trained dt_emb 的初始 performance）。\n      在 worst 档下这被解释为：frozen dt_emb 不是 viable mitigation（too costly），且该结果仅在 Walker 中\n      observeable——在 Cheetah/Cartpole 中 frozen 与 trained 的差异更小因为 dt_emb 本身 less impactful。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"015 frozen dt_emb result\"\n        columns: [metric, value, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [\"eval_105K\", 204, \"22% baseline (severe degradation)\"]\n          - [\"nve_peak\", 0.47, \"far below 1.5x (no CIVO)\"]\n          - [\"actor_loss\", \"→0\", \"gradient starvation\"]\n          - [\"collapse\", \"no\", \"stable but low-performing\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"015 vs 008d vs baseline: frozen avoids CIVO but at extreme performance cost\"\n    analysis: >\n      Confirms dt_emb TRAINING is necessary for CIVO in Walker。但 worst 档论点：\n      这只在 Walker 中 informative，因为其他 envs 即使 TRAINED dt_emb 也不触发 CIVO。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 additional seeds (seed 3-4)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"Narrow true collapse probability of 008e_v3\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed3_eval_105K: 780\n      seed3_collapse: false\n      seed3_nve_peak: 0.85\n      seed4_eval_105K: 190\n      seed4_collapse: true\n      seed4_nve_105K: 2.95\n      seed4_collapse_mechanism: \"mixed (Pathway A onset at 95K)\"\n      total_collapse_rate: \"2/4 (50%)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档指定 walker_additional_seeds_nve_separation=[0.75,1.0]，意味着 additional seeds 可能\n      显示分离度略降。2/4 collapse rate (50%) 与 008d 的 collapse rate 相同——dt=1 imagination\n      未提供任何保护。更糟的是，seed 4 的崩溃可能展示 mixed dynamics（既有 value overestimation\n      又有 eval-driven instability），模糊 Pathway A/B 的 clean distinction。这在 worst 档下\n      被解读为：Walker Walk 中 trained dt_emb 的 vulnerability 是 multi-modal 的，不可简单归因于\n      单一 CIVO mechanism。50% collapse rate 本身可能是 Walker 的 reward landscape property\n      （~50% 的 initial condition 导致 late-stage instability），与 dt_emb 的 interaction 可能是\n      coincidental 而非 causal。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008e_v3 full 4-seed summary\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_105K, collapse, nve_peak, pathway]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 870, \"no\", 0.80, \"healthy\"]\n          - [2, 137, \"yes\", 3.78, \"Pathway B (eval-driven)\"]\n          - [3, 780, \"no\", 0.85, \"healthy\"]\n          - [4, 190, \"yes\", 2.95, \"mixed A/B\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-seed 008e_v3 eval trajectories: bimodal outcome (healthy ~800 or collapse ~150-190)\"\n    analysis: >\n      50% collapse rate 与 008d 相同 → dt=1 imagination mitigation 完全无效。Worst 档下此结果\n      进一步削弱 paper 的 prescriptive value。且 seed 4 的 mixed mechanism 模糊了 clean causal story。\n\n  - name: \"Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_060\"\n    description: \"Truncate imagination when RSSM prediction uncertainty exceeds threshold\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_105K: 520\n      vs_baseline: \"-45%\"\n      nve_peak: 1.35\n      collapse: false\n      truncation_rate_at_dt2: 0.65\n      effective_horizon: 5.2\n      vs_008d_improvement: \"+55% (520 vs 82.7@55K)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Uncertainty-gating 在 Walker 中部分有效（避免 collapse），但大幅截断 imagination（65% of dt=2\n      rollouts 被 truncate），导致 effective horizon 仅 5.2 steps（vs planned 15）。Eval 在 baseline\n      的 55% 水平——比 collapse 好但远低于 baseline。在 worst 档下这被解释为：(1) mitigation 在 Walker\n      中 works 但 cost 高（45% eval loss from truncation）；(2) 这种 mitigation 在 Cheetah/Cartpole 中\n      无意义因为不需要 truncation（CIVO 不存在）；(3) 无法判断 improvement 是来自 uncertainty-gating 本身\n      还是仅仅是因为 truncation 导致 shorter effective dt（approaching dt=1 naturally）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Uncertainty-gated pilot results\"\n        columns: [metric, value, vs_baseline, vs_008d]\n        rows:\n          - [\"eval_105K\", 520, \"-45%\", \"+528%\"]\n          - [\"nve_peak\", 1.35, \"N/A\", \"-35%\"]\n          - [\"truncation_rate\", \"65%\", \"N/A\", \"N/A\"]\n          - [\"effective_horizon\", 5.2, \"-65% of H=15\", \"N/A\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Uncertainty-gated eval trajectory with truncation rate overlay\"\n    analysis: >\n      Partial success in Walker but the improvement is likely explained by de facto horizon reduction\n      (5.2 ≈ H=5 → less exposure to dt>1 errors)。Not a principled solution; cross-env 无意义。\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: \"Third DMC environment for generalization — worst tier predicts no CIVO\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_mean_eval: 250\n      trained_dtEmb_mean_eval: 210\n      trained_dtEmb_nve_peak: 1.05\n      trained_dtEmb_vs_baseline: \"-16%\"\n      no_dtEmb_mean_eval: 205\n      collapse_count: \"0/3\"\n      nve_above_1.5x: \"0/3\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Hopper Hop 在 DreamerV3 中本身表现中等 (baseline ~200-300)。Worst 档预测与 Cheetah/Cartpole\n      一致：trained dt_emb 不触发 CIVO (nve<1.3x)，degradation 仅 16%（subsample 效应），\n      与 no_dtEmb 不可区分。进一步确认 CIVO 是 Walker-specific artifact。\n      Hopper 的 reward landscape 涉及 hop height + forward progress，虽然 nonlinear 但 Hopper\n      的 low baseline performance (250) 意味着 value estimates 的 absolute magnitude 小，\n      即使有 overestimation 也不足以形成正反馈（critic 的 absolute error 太小 to dominate actor gradient）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Hopper Hop summary (worst tier)\"\n        columns: [config, mean_eval_300K, nve_peak, collapse_rate]\n        rows:\n          - [\"baseline\", 250, \"N/A (reference)\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"trained dt_emb + sub ON\", 210, 1.05, \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"no dt_emb + sub ON\", 205, 0.80, \"0/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-environment summary: only Walker shows CIVO — environment-specific artifact\"\n    analysis: >\n      Fourth environment confirming CIVO non-replication。At this point the evidence is overwhelming：\n      Walker Walk 是 CIVO 能被观察到的唯一环境。论文必须 reframe 为 \"boundary conditions\" paper。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run exp_018 (Full-SGS) extrapolation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030 (related)\"\n    description: \"Full stop-gradient on obs decoders → dt_emb 仅保留 7% KL gradient\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_full_sgs_eval_105K: 160\n      walker_full_sgs_nve_peak: 0.55\n      walker_full_sgs_collapse: false\n      walker_full_sgs_actor_loss: \"→0 (gradient starvation)\"\n      mechanism: \"obs decoder detach kills 93% of dt_emb gradient → effectively frozen\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Full-SGS 移除 93% of dt_emb gradient (obs decoders)，仅保留 7% KL dynamics gradient。\n      效果类似 frozen dt_emb (plan_015)：CIVO 被 eliminate 但 performance 严重退化，因为\n      dt_emb 几乎不训练 → 与 015b 的 gradient starvation 相似。在 worst 档下，Full-SGS 是\n      另一个 \"过度干预\" 方案：解决了 CIVO 但 payoff 为负（eval 远低于 baseline）。\n      且此干预仅在 Walker 中 relevant——其他环境没有 CIVO 需要 prevent。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"SGS variants comparison (Walker)\"\n        columns: [config, eval_105K, nve_peak, collapse, mechanism]\n        rows:\n          - [\"016e (reward SGS only)\", \"31.7@95K\", 10.42, \"yes\", \"no-op (reward grad=0)\"]\n          - [\"018 (Full-SGS: obs detach)\", 160, 0.55, \"no\", \"gradient starvation\"]\n          - [\"015b (frozen dt_emb)\", 204, 0.47, \"no\", \"gradient starvation\"]\n          - [\"008d (no intervention)\", \"82.7@55K\", 4.12, \"yes\", \"classic CIVO\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"SGS intervention spectrum: from no-op (016e) to over-kill (018/015b)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Full-SGS and frozen dt_emb produce similar outcomes: CIVO prevented but performance destroyed.\n      No middle ground found. In worst tier this is: \"the only interventions that prevent CIVO in Walker\n      also destroy learning — suggesting the trained dt_emb is load-bearing for what learning does occur.\"\n\n  - name: \"Cross-environment NVE threshold diagnostic validation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_034\"\n    description: \"Formal statistical evaluation of nve>1.5x as universal CIVO diagnostic\"\n    expected_results:\n      classification_matrix:\n        walker_TP: 4\n        walker_FN: 0\n        walker_TN: 4\n        walker_FP: 0\n        cheetah_TP: 0\n        cheetah_FN: 3\n        cheetah_TN: 3\n        cheetah_FP: 0\n        cartpole_TP: 0\n        cartpole_FN: 3\n        cartpole_TN: 3\n        cartpole_FP: 0\n      overall_sensitivity: 0.40\n      overall_specificity: 1.0\n      overall_accuracy: 0.70\n      cross_env_auroc: 0.58\n      conclusion: \"Threshold is Walker-specific; fails as universal diagnostic\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cross-env 分析的核心问题：threshold 的 specificity 完美 (1.0) 因为 untrained dt_emb 从不\n      exceed 1.5x（在所有环境中一致）。但 sensitivity 仅 40% 因为 Cheetah+Cartpole 的 trained dt_emb\n      也不 exceed 1.5x。如果我们将 \"trained dt_emb\" 定义为 \"should trigger CIVO\"，那么 6/10 trained\n      cases 是 false negatives。AUROC 0.58 接近 random (0.5)。这证明 nve>1.5x 不是 architectural\n      vulnerability marker，而是 Walker-Walk-specific pathology marker。Diagnostic 的适用范围\n      必须被 explicitly bounded。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-env diagnostic evaluation\"\n        columns: [metric, walker_only, all_envs, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Sensitivity\", \"1.0 (4/4)\", \"0.40 (4/10)\", \"fails cross-env\"]\n          - [\"Specificity\", \"1.0 (4/4)\", \"1.0 (10/10)\", \"high (vacuously)\"]\n          - [\"AUROC\", 1.0, 0.58, \"near-random cross-env\"]\n          - [\"PPV\", \"1.0\", \"1.0\", \"if positive, always correct\"]\n          - [\"NPV\", \"1.0\", \"0.63\", \"if negative, 37% chance missed CIVO\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ROC curve overlay: Walker-only (AUC=1.0) vs all-envs (AUC=0.58)\"\n    analysis: >\n      NVE>1.5x 作为 universal diagnostic 的 cross-env validity 被 falsified。\n      论文必须将其定位为 \"environment-conditional diagnostic\" 并提供 applicability criteria\n      (reward nonlinearity > X, obs_dim > Y, reward_gap > 2.0x)。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb) seeds 1-2 — boundary condition\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Additional context for worst-tier reframing\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 680\n      seed1_nve_range: [0.55, 0.80]\n      seed2_eval_105K: 550\n      seed2_nve_range: [0.60, 0.85]\n      cross_seed_eval_cv: 0.15\n      interpretation: \"Value suppression consistent but eval benefit variable\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档的 reframing 中，008a 的 additional seeds 显示 value suppression 在 Walker 内\n      robust (all nve<1.0x) 但 eval 表现 variable (550-778, CV=15%)。这削弱了 \"untrained dt_emb =\n      practical solution\" 的叙事——protection 有效但 performance 代价 unpredictable (15-40% below baseline)。\n      Worst 档将此解释为：即使在 Walker Walk 这个 CIVO 最强的环境中，mitigation 的 benefit/cost tradeoff\n      也是 uncertain。在不存在 CIVO 的其他环境中，untrained dt_emb 纯粹是 unnecessary overhead。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008a multi-seed (Walker only, worst tier context)\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_105K, nve_range, vs_baseline, trend]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 778, \"0.59-0.93\", \"-15%\", \"zigzag recovery, best case\"]\n          - [1, 680, \"0.55-0.80\", \"-26%\", \"moderate recovery\"]\n          - [2, 550, \"0.60-0.85\", \"-40%\", \"slow, still below 75K peak\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"008a 3-seed with IQM: large CI band undermines 'near-baseline' claim\"\n    analysis: >\n      IQM across 3 seeds: ~670 (-27% baseline)。原 seed 0 的 778 是上界 outlier。\n      Worst 档利用此修正 C3 claim 的强度从 \"85% baseline\" 到 \"60-85% baseline (IQM ~73%)\"。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41066,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41066},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"804c4c93-33c8-4f5e-98da-2ef3e29caf63","uuid":"1573a400-6fc0-4d47-bc35-4b851c4f7047"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":359969,"duration_api_ms":361871,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Reframe from 'architectural vulnerability of imagination-based AC' to 'interaction between reward landscape geometry\n  and dt-conditioning in world models'. CIVO is a real failure mode in specific task-architecture combinations — Walker Walk\n  exposes it due to smooth reward gradient + locomotion dynamics + particular state space geometry. Cross-environment\n  experiments reveal CIVO requires particular conditions to manifest: Cheetah Run's reward landscape is too noisy/steep\n  for the overestimation feedback loop to lock in; Cartpole Swingup's low-dimensional state space prevents the observation\n  decoder from driving dt_emb gradient amplification. TAWM contrast reframed as 'MPC robustness may come from planning\n  horizon truncation, not architecture per se'. Core contribution: cautionary tale about benchmark-specific findings in\n  MBRL — the mechanism is real but prevalence depends on task properties (reward smoothness, state dimensionality,\n  locomotion dynamics). Supplement with Walker factorial (still strong: causal chain intact) as complete case study +\n  Cheetah/Cartpole as negative transfer cases revealing boundary conditions. Still targets CoRL — diagnostic papers\n  showing when something does/doesn't work are valuable, but claims must be explicitly bounded to Walker-like environments.\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"Replicate delusional critic collapse with 2 more seeds in Walker Walk\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_nve_peak: 1.73\n      seed1_nve_peak_step: 45K\n      seed1_collapse: true\n      seed1_eval_105K: 131\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.62\n      seed2_nve_peak_step: 45K\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 268\n      nve_above_1.5x_count: \"2/2\"\n      collapse_rate: \"1/2\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Walker Walk 已知在 worst 档下仍然展示 CIVO（worst 档的定义是跨环境失败，不是 Walker 本身失败）。\n      walker_additional_seeds_nve_separation=[0.75,1.0] 意味着在更多 seed 下分离度略降但 Walker 内部\n      仍保持 nve>1.5x。既有数据（009e collapsed@55K nve=4.12x, 009b self-corrected@268 nve_peak=1.62x）\n      已经确认了这个模式。Collapse 是 stochastic (1/2)，但 pathological overestimation (nve>1.5x) 是 reliable (2/2)。\n      这些结果与 worst 档兼容因为 worst 档的核心论点是\"Walker 是特殊的\"而非\"Walker 也不 work\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Walker 008d multi-seed summary\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, nve_peak_step, collapse, eval_105K, mechanism]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 4.12, 55K, \"yes\", 82.7, \"classic CIVO: value explosion\"]\n          - [1, 1.73, 45K, \"yes (same as seed 0)\", 131, \"sustained nve>1.5x → collapse\"]\n          - [2, 2.05, 25K, \"no (self-corrected)\", 268, \"transient nve>1.5x → recovery\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"NVE trajectory plot: all 3 seeds overlaid showing 100% exceed 1.5x, divergence point between collapse/recovery\"\n    analysis: >\n      Walker 内 nve>1.5x threshold 保持 100% separating power。但这在 worst 档下被重新解释为\n      Walker-specific phenomenon：该环境的 smooth reward gradient 允许 value overestimation\n      正反馈循环锁定，而非通用架构脆弱性。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control stability with 2 more seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_nve_peak: 1.02\n      seed1_nve_peak_step: 25K\n      seed1_eval_105K: 503\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.26\n      seed2_nve_peak_step: 25K\n      seed2_eval_105K: 148\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      nve_above_1.5x_count: \"0/2\"\n      separation_vs_008d: \"4/4 (trained 2/2 > 1.5x, untrained 0/2 < 1.5x)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      008f 在 worst 档下仍然显示 no CIVO（nve<1.5x），因为 worst 档的问题不在于 Walker 因果链断裂，\n      而在于该因果链无法泛化。dt_embed_dim=0 的保护机制在 Walker 内一致有效。但 seed 2 (009c) 已显示\n      持续衰退 (359→148@105K)，这削弱了 008f 作为\"稳定\"控制的叙事——它避免了 CIVO 但带来了其他退化\n      （reward prediction 质量差 75x，长期 eval 衰退）。Worst 档利用此发现论证：即便在 Walker 内，\n      causal control 的\"保护\"也是 fragile 的——seed 2 的 eval 持续下降 (nve=1.14@105K approaching boundary)\n      暗示更长训练可能突破 1.5x threshold。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Walker 008f multi-seed summary\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, eval_peak, eval_105K, trend]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 1.02, 503, 503, \"zigzag recovery\"]\n          - [1, 1.26, 359, 148, \"decline after 75K peak\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"008f dual-seed eval trajectory: divergent outcomes (recovery vs decline) despite identical config\"\n    analysis: >\n      008f 的 cross-seed inconsistency (503 vs 148@105K) 在 worst 档下被解读为：即使消除 CIVO，\n      dt>1 training 本身引入的学习难度使结果高度 stochastic。这支持\"reward landscape geometry 主导\"的论点。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 (mitigation) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"Multi-seed validation of dt=1 imagination as mitigation\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 870\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.80\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 137\n      seed2_nve_105K: 3.78\n      seed2_collapse: true\n      seed2_collapse_mechanism: \"eval-driven policy instability (Pathway B)\"\n      collapse_rate: \"1/2 (50%)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有数据完全匹配 worst 档预期。008e_v3 s2 的崩溃（非 CIVO 机制，entropy↑ 而非↓）在 worst 档下\n      被解释为：trained dt_embedding 在 Walker Walk 的 reward landscape 下创造多条 instability 通路，\n      这是 task-specific interaction 而非通用架构缺陷。dt=1 imagination 消除了 Pathway A (CIVO)\n      但 Pathway B (policy instability) 是 Walker Walk 特定 reward structure 与 trained dt_emb 的\n      interaction artifact。在 Cheetah/Cartpole 中 Pathway B 也不存在。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008e_v3 collapse mechanism comparison\"\n        columns: [seed, collapse, mechanism, nve_driver, entropy_trend]\n        rows:\n          - [1, \"no\", \"healthy\", \"eval growth → nve stable\", \"monotone decreasing\"]\n          - [2, \"yes\", \"Pathway B (non-CIVO)\", \"eval crash → nve spike\", \"increasing (destabilization)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"008e_v3 dual pathway diagram: seed 1 healthy vs seed 2 Pathway B collapse dynamics\"\n    analysis: >\n      50% collapse rate 与 008d 相同，worst 档解读为 Walker Walk 的 reward landscape geometry\n      inherently 导致 ~50% 的训练 trajectory 在 late stage 进入不稳定区域（当有 trained dt_emb 时）。\n      这不是 CIVO-specific 而是 task-architecture interaction。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression with 2 more seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 680\n      seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.65\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 550\n      seed2_normalized_ve_105K: 0.72\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      cross_seed_ve_range: [0.55, 0.80]\n      vs_baseline_range: [-28%, -40%]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Untrained dt_emb 在 Walker 内保持 value suppression（normalized_ve < 1.0x）。但 worst 档\n      下 additional seeds 显示更大 variance：seed 0 达到 778 (85% baseline) 可能是幸运的高点。\n      新 seeds 可能在 550-680 范围（60-74% baseline），而非 seed 0 的 85%。这降低了 008a 作为\n      \"near-baseline mitigation\" 的说服力——untrained dt_emb 保护了 CIVO 但引入 15-40% eval penalty，\n      且 penalty 幅度 seed-dependent。Worst 档利用此 weaken \"untrained dt_emb = protection\" narrative。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Walker 008a multi-seed\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_105K, normalized_ve_105K, vs_baseline, trend]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 778, 0.59, \"-15%\", \"zigzag recovery to new high\"]\n          - [1, 680, 0.65, \"-26%\", \"zigzag, lower plateau\"]\n          - [2, 550, 0.72, \"-40%\", \"slower convergence, still rising\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"008a 3-seed eval trajectories with IQM + 95% CI\"\n    analysis: >\n      Value suppression 在 Walker 内 robust (all seeds nve<1.0x)，但 eval 最终表现的 inter-seed variance\n      较大 (550-778, CV=15%)。Worst 档下这被解释为\"保护有效但 benefit 幅度不确定\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in second DMC environment for cross-environment validation\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_500K: 680\n      seed2_eval_500K: 590\n      seed3_eval_500K: 720\n      mean_final_eval: 663\n      inter_seed_std: 66\n      inter_seed_cv: 0.10\n      ve_ratio_stable: 0.55-0.68\n      peak_eval: 732\n      convergence_step: 200K\n      baseline_noise_level: \"moderate (10% CV)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档指定 cheetah_baseline_final_eval=[500,750]。Cheetah Run 在 DreamerV3 中的典型表现\n      是 600-800 range，但 inter-seed variance 通常高于 Walker Walk（Cheetah 的 reward landscape\n      更 noisy，有多个 local optima 对应不同 gait patterns）。10% inter-seed CV 使得 20% degradation\n      threshold 与正常 variance 重叠，削弱对照实验的 statistical power。exp_010a 已在 312K 达到 657.9\n      (peak 732.9@265K)，与此预测一致。Baseline 本身不 pathological 但 variance 足够大使得后续\n      degradation 信号被 noise 淹没。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_200K, eval_300K, eval_500K, peak, ve_stable]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 620, 680, 680, 733, 0.62]\n          - [2, 510, 570, 590, 615, 0.58]\n          - [3, 650, 710, 720, 740, 0.65]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah baseline learning curves: moderate inter-seed variance, slower convergence than Walker\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 的 10% CV 和 500-750 range 为 worst 档设置了关键前提：当 trained dt_emb 的\n      degradation 仅 0-20% 时，差异落入 baseline noise band，无法达到统计显著。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: \"Attempt to replicate CIVO in Cheetah Run — worst tier predicts failure\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 580\n      seed1_nve_peak: 1.15\n      seed1_nve_peak_step: 55K\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 520\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.28\n      seed2_nve_peak_step: 45K\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed3_eval_105K: 610\n      seed3_nve_peak: 0.95\n      seed3_nve_peak_step: 35K\n      seed3_collapse: false\n      mean_eval_105K: 570\n      vs_baseline_at_105K: \"-12%\"\n      nve_above_1.5x_count: \"0/3\"\n      collapse_count: \"0/3\"\n      max_nve_across_seeds: 1.28\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心假设：cheetah_trained_dtEmb_nve_peak=[0.8,1.3]。CIVO 不触发的机制解释：\n      (1) Cheetah Run 的 reward function 是 velocity-based (near-linear in forward speed)，\n      不像 Walker Walk 有复杂的 balance/posture 组件。RSSM 在 dt=2 时的 observation prediction error\n      主要影响 velocity magnitude 预测，但 reward ≈ linear(velocity)，使得 observation error 不会\n      被非线性放大为 reward overestimation。(2) Cheetah 的 24-dim observation space 更低维，\n      observation decoder 对 dt_emb 的梯度驱动更弱（Walker 的 orientations/velocity/height 复合体\n      为 dt_emb 提供了更丰富的梯度信号）。(3) Eval degradation 仅 12%——在 baseline 10% CV 的背景下，\n      这与 noise 不可区分。dt_emb 确实学到了 dt=1 vs dt=2 的区分（reward gap >1.5x），但 critic\n      未能形成加速正反馈循环因为 value overestimation 不 compound（reward too linear）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah trained dt_emb CIVO analysis\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, nve_peak_step, eval_105K, vs_baseline, collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 1.15, 55K, 580, \"-8%\", \"no\"]\n          - [2, 1.28, 45K, 520, \"-17%\", \"no\"]\n          - [3, 0.95, 35K, 610, \"-5%\", \"no\"]\n      - name: \"Cross-environment NVE comparison\"\n        columns: [environment, trained_dtEmb_nve_peak_mean, nve_above_1.5x_rate, collapse_rate]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", 2.59, \"4/4 (100%)\", \"2/4 (50%)\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", 1.13, \"0/3 (0%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah vs Walker NVE trajectories: Walker shows acceleration past 1.5x; Cheetah plateaus below 1.3x\"\n      - \"Reward landscape comparison: Walker nonlinear (balance) vs Cheetah near-linear (velocity)\"\n    analysis: >\n      CIVO 完全未触发。nve 从未接近 1.5x threshold。12% mean degradation 在 baseline CV=10% 下\n      不显著 (p>0.3, Mann-Whitney)。这是 worst 档最核心的 negative result：CIVO mechanism 的\n      reward-geometry dependence 暴露。Walker 的 nonlinear reward (balance + locomotion composite)\n      允许 observation error 被非线性放大；Cheetah 的 near-linear reward 不提供此放大。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: \"Causal control in Cheetah — expected to be indistinguishable from trained dt_emb\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 550\n      seed1_nve_peak: 0.90\n      seed2_eval_105K: 540\n      seed2_nve_peak: 0.85\n      seed3_eval_105K: 600\n      seed3_nve_peak: 0.92\n      mean_eval_105K: 563\n      vs_baseline_at_105K: \"-15%\"\n      vs_plan021_difference: \"-1% (not significant)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 Cheetah Run 中，trained dt_emb (plan_021) 本身未导致 CIVO，所以 dt_embed_dim=0 的\n      \"保护\"效果无法被观测到——两组的 eval 和 nve 轨迹统计上不可区分。这是 worst 档的直接推论：\n      如果 disease 不存在，cure 就无法展示 efficacy。Eval 都在 baseline 的 noise band 内\n      (-5% to -17%)，差异由 subsampling 本身的 learning signal reduction 主导而非 dt_emb。\n      这摧毁了 \"dt_embed_dim=0 → stable\" 作为通用因果证据的论述——它在 Cheetah 中是 vacuously true。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah causal control comparison\"\n        columns: [config, mean_eval_105K, mean_nve_peak, vs_baseline]\n        rows:\n          - [\"trained dt_emb (021)\", 570, 1.13, \"-12%\"]\n          - [\"dt_embed_dim=0 (022)\", 563, 0.89, \"-15%\"]\n          - [\"p-value (Mann-Whitney)\", null, null, \"0.78 (n.s.)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah 021 vs 022: overlapping confidence intervals, no causal separation\"\n    analysis: >\n      因果控制实验在 Cheetah 中失效——不是因为控制失败，而是因为 treatment (trained dt_emb) 本身无效。\n      NVE threshold 作为 diagnostic 在 Cheetah 中 vacuously true for both conditions (all <1.5x)，\n      separating power = 0/6 (无 positive 可 separate)。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: \"Value growth suppression test in Cheetah\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 600\n      seed1_normalized_ve: 0.85\n      seed2_eval_105K: 560\n      seed2_normalized_ve: 0.80\n      seed3_eval_105K: 640\n      seed3_normalized_ve: 0.88\n      mean_eval_105K: 600\n      vs_baseline_at_105K: \"-5%\"\n      vs_plan021_difference: \"+5% (marginal)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Untrained dt_emb + no subsample 在 Cheetah 中表现与 baseline 接近（-5%），略优于 trained dt_emb\n      config (-12%)。但差异 marginal (5%, within noise)。Worst 档解读：在不存在 CIVO 的环境中，\n      untrained dt_emb 的 \"保护\" 效果仅反映 subsample OFF 保留了完整 learning signal（plan_021\n      有 subsample ON 导致的 50% signal loss），而非 value suppression 的功效。\n      Normalized ve 在 0.80-0.88 范围——与 trained dt_emb 的 0.85-1.15 重叠。\n      \"Value growth suppression\" 叙事在 Cheetah 中不成立，因为根本没有需要 suppress 的 pathological growth。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah value suppression test\"\n        columns: [config, mean_eval_105K, mean_nve, vs_baseline, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [\"untrained+no_sub (023)\", 600, 0.84, \"-5%\", \"normal\"]\n          - [\"trained+sub_ON (021)\", 570, 1.13, \"-12%\", \"normal (mild degradation from subsample)\"]\n          - [\"no_embed+sub_ON (022)\", 563, 0.89, \"-15%\", \"normal\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah 3-config comparison: all within noise band, no CIVO signature in any\"\n    analysis: >\n      三组 Cheetah 配置的差异完全由 subsample 解释，与 dt_emb 无关。Untrained dt_emb 没有\n      展示 Walker 中观察到的 structural value suppression pattern。\n\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: \"Measure RSSM fidelity gap across environments\"\n    expected_results:\n      cheetah_baseline_obs_gap: 1.75\n      cheetah_008d_obs_gap: 1.45\n      cheetah_008d_reward_gap: 1.35\n      cheetah_008f_reward_gap: 1.02\n      walker_008d_reward_gap: 2.78\n      cheetah_vs_walker_reward_gap_ratio: 0.49\n      cheetah_008d_dt1_obs_mse: 18.5\n      cheetah_008d_dt2_obs_mse: 26.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah 的 RSSM fidelity gap 显著小于 Walker。Reward gap 1.35x (vs Walker 2.78x) 因为\n      Cheetah reward ≈ linear(velocity)，即使 observation prediction error 存在，线性映射限制了\n      reward prediction divergence。Walker 的 reward function 涉及 upright posture + forward velocity\n      的复合，RSSM 在 dt=2 时的 observation error 通过非线性 reward mapping 被放大为 2.78x reward gap。\n      这是 CIVO 环境依赖性的 mechanistic root cause：reward function 的非线性程度决定了 observation error\n      到 value overestimation 的放大系数。Cheetah 的放大系数 ~1.35x 不足以驱动正反馈循环。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-environment RSSM fidelity\"\n        columns: [env, model, dt1_obs_mse, dt2_obs_mse, obs_gap, dt1_reward_mae, dt2_reward_mae, reward_gap]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker\", \"008d (trained)\", 41.31, 53.67, 1.30, 0.0568, 0.1579, 2.78]\n          - [\"Walker\", \"008f (no embed)\", 8.01, 22.04, 2.75, 0.7469, 0.7526, 1.01]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", \"trained dt_emb\", 18.5, 26.8, 1.45, 0.032, 0.043, 1.35]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", \"no dt_emb\", 12.2, 24.1, 1.98, 0.52, 0.53, 1.02]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Reward gap vs NVE peak scatter: Walker high reward_gap → high nve; Cheetah low reward_gap → low nve\"\n    analysis: >\n      Reward gap 与 NVE peak 强相关 (r=0.92)。Walker 的 2.78x reward gap 产生 nve>1.5x；\n      Cheetah 的 1.35x reward gap 产生 nve<1.3x。这是 environment-specificity 的 mechanistic 证据。\n      论文需要明确：CIVO 需要 reward_gap > ~2.0x 才能触发正反馈循环。\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: \"Plot actor_entropy for healthy vs collapsed configs\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_entropy_decline: \"-0.195 to -4.88 (35K→55K)\"\n      walker_008a_entropy_stable: \"-3.5 to -4.2 (steady)\"\n      cheetah_trained_dtEmb_entropy: \"-3.8 to -4.5 (normal decline, no pathology)\"\n      cheetah_no_dtEmb_entropy: \"-3.6 to -4.3 (indistinguishable from trained)\"\n      entropy_divergence_point_walker: 35K\n      entropy_divergence_point_cheetah: \"none (no divergence)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Walker 中 collapsed configs (008d) 显示 entropy 急剧下降（actor 变得过度 deterministic，\n      锁定 delusional policy）。Cheetah 中 trained dt_emb 的 entropy trajectory 与 no_dtEmb 和\n      baseline 无统计差异——因为 actor 从未收到 delusional critic gradient signal，所以不存在\n      exploitation-driven entropy collapse。这进一步确认 CIVO feedback loop 在 Cheetah 中未激活。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Actor entropy comparison\"\n        columns: [env, config, entropy_35K, entropy_55K, entropy_105K, divergence]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker\", \"008d (collapse)\", -3.47, -4.88, \"N/A (collapsed@55K)\", \"strong divergence@35K\"]\n          - [\"Walker\", \"008a (healthy)\", -3.2, -3.8, -4.1, \"none\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", \"trained dt_emb\", -3.1, -3.8, -4.3, \"none\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", \"no dt_emb\", -3.0, -3.6, -4.2, \"none\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-panel entropy plot: Walker shows clear bifurcation; Cheetah shows no bifurcation\"\n    analysis: >\n      Entropy analysis 在 Cheetah 中完全阴性。No divergence between trained/untrained dt_emb。\n      This is consistent with CIVO not activating — no delusional gradient → no policy exploitation → no entropy collapse。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: \"Distribution plots of V(s) vs Monte Carlo return\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_value_bias_mean: \"+45% (systematic overestimation)\"\n      walker_008d_value_bias_skew: 1.8\n      cheetah_trained_dtEmb_value_bias_mean: \"+8% (within normal calibration error)\"\n      cheetah_trained_dtEmb_value_bias_skew: 0.3\n      walker_008a_value_bias_mean: \"-12% (conservative)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Walker 008d 展示系统性 right-skewed overestimation (mean V > mean MC-return by 45%)；\n      Cheetah trained dt_emb 展示 well-calibrated distribution (bias 仅 8%，skew 接近 0)。\n      这直接可视化了 CIVO 在两个环境中的有/无：Walker 的 value distribution 与 realized returns\n      完全脱钩（right tail explosion），Cheetah 的 value 保持 calibrated。差异不是 degree 而是 kind。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 histogram grid: (Walker/Cheetah) × (trained/untrained dt_emb) V(s) vs MC-return\"\n      - \"Q-Q plots showing Walker 008d deviation from diagonal; Cheetah on diagonal\"\n    analysis: >\n      Distributional evidence 最清晰地展示 environment-specificity：Walker 008d 的 value 分布\n      与 MC-return 完全不 overlap（pathological）；Cheetah 的 value 分布紧贴 MC-return（healthy）。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: \"Analyze learned dt_embedding vectors evolution\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_dt1_dt2_cosine_early: 0.95\n      walker_dt1_dt2_cosine_late: 0.45\n      cheetah_dt1_dt2_cosine_early: 0.93\n      cheetah_dt1_dt2_cosine_late: 0.72\n      walker_embedding_separation_rate: \"0.01/1K steps\"\n      cheetah_embedding_separation_rate: \"0.004/1K steps\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      两环境的 dt_embedding 都学会了区分 dt=1/dt=2（cosine<1.0），但 Walker 的分离度更大（0.45 vs 0.72）。\n      这反映了 Walker 中 observation decoder 向 dt_emb 提供了更强的梯度（93% of grad norm from obs decoders），\n      驱动 embedding 快速分离。Cheetah 的 lower-dimensional obs space 提供更弱的梯度，embedding 分离\n      更慢更温和。Embedding 分离本身不是 pathological——问题是 Walker 中高分离度 + nonlinear reward\n      形成了 CIVO；Cheetah 中温和分离度 + linear reward 不触发 CIVO。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"dt_embedding separation dynamics\"\n        columns: [env, cosine_5K, cosine_25K, cosine_55K, cosine_105K, separation_rate]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker\", 0.95, 0.78, 0.52, 0.45, \"0.01/1K\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", 0.93, 0.85, 0.76, 0.72, \"0.004/1K\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cosine similarity decay curve: Walker rapid separation vs Cheetah gradual\"\n    analysis: >\n      Embedding separation rate 与 obs_decoder gradient magnitude 相关。Walker 的高 separation\n      是 CIVO 的 enabler（gives critic precise but wrong dt>1 information），但不是 sufficient cause。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_050\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in non-locomotion environment\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_500K: 820\n      seed2_eval_500K: 790\n      seed3_eval_500K: 845\n      mean_final_eval: 818\n      inter_seed_cv: 0.03\n      ve_ratio_stable: 0.65-0.72\n      convergence_step: 100K\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole Swingup 是低维任务 (5-dim obs, 1-dim action)，DreamerV3 通常快速收敛到高性能。\n      Inter-seed variance 低 (CV<5%) 因为 task 简单、reward landscape smooth、optimal policy 几乎唯一。\n      这为 cross-env comparison 提供了高 signal-to-noise baseline。但 worst 档预测即使 trained dt_emb\n      也不会在此环境触发 CIVO，因为 obs space 太小无法为 dt_emb 提供足够梯度。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_100K, eval_300K, eval_500K, ve_stable]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 720, 810, 820, 0.68]\n          - [2, 690, 780, 790, 0.66]\n          - [3, 740, 830, 845, 0.71]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole baseline: fast convergence, tight inter-seed band\"\n    analysis: >\n      Clean baseline establishes that Cartpole has very low stochasticity (CV=3%)。\n      This makes any degradation signal detectable — but worst tier predicts no degradation to detect。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_051\"\n    description: \"CIVO test in Cartpole — worst tier predicts complete absence\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 680\n      seed1_nve_peak: 0.95\n      seed2_eval_105K: 700\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.10\n      seed3_eval_105K: 660\n      seed3_nve_peak: 0.88\n      mean_eval_105K: 680\n      vs_baseline_at_105K: \"-10%\"\n      nve_above_1.5x_count: \"0/3\"\n      collapse_count: \"0/3\"\n      max_nve: 1.10\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心假设：cartpole_trained_dtEmb_nve_peak=[0.7,1.2]。CIVO 不触发的机制：\n      (1) 5-dim observation space 太小 — dt_emb.weight 的 gradient norm 中 obs_decoder 贡献\n      远低于 Walker (Walker 有 24+ dim with orientations/velocities/height)。Gradient starvation\n      使 dt_emb 无法学到足够 precise 的 dt-conditioning 来 exploit。\n      (2) Cartpole reward = balance (angle) + height，虽然 nonlinear 但 low-dimensional nonlinearity\n      不足以产生 Walker 级别的 reward gap amplification。\n      (3) RSSM 在 low-dim system 中预测 dt=2 的 fidelity gap 更小（fewer dimensions to get wrong）。\n      结果：10% eval degradation（来自 subsampling 的 learning signal loss）但 NO value pathology。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole CIVO test\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak, eval_105K, vs_baseline, collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 0.95, 680, \"-7%\", \"no\"]\n          - [2, 1.10, 700, \"-4%\", \"no\"]\n          - [3, 0.88, 660, \"-10%\", \"no\"]\n      - name: \"Cross-environment CIVO summary (worst tier)\"\n        columns: [env, obs_dim, trained_dtEmb_nve_peak, nve_1.5x_rate, collapse_rate, mechanism_active]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"24+\", 2.59, \"4/4\", \"2/4\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"17\", 1.13, \"0/3\", \"0/3\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", \"5\", 0.98, \"0/3\", \"0/3\", \"NO\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-environment NVE comparison: only Walker exceeds 1.5x threshold\"\n      - \"NVE peak vs obs_dim scatter: positive correlation suggesting dimensionality dependence\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cartpole 是最极端的 negative case。Trained dt_emb 几乎不影响 value dynamics (nve 0.88-1.10x,\n      normal calibration range)。CIVO mechanism 完全 inert。10% eval loss 来自 subsampling 不足。\n      Cross-env NVE threshold accuracy: Walker 4/4 + Cheetah 0/0(no positives) + Cartpole 0/0(no positives)\n      → threshold 在 non-Walker envs 中 vacuously satisfied (no positives to classify)。\n      实际 diagnostic 价值为 0。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_052\"\n    description: \"Causal control in Cartpole — predicted indistinguishable from trained\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 670\n      seed2_eval_105K: 690\n      seed3_eval_105K: 650\n      mean_eval_105K: 670\n      vs_plan051_difference: \"-1.5% (not significant, p=0.85)\"\n      nve_peak_mean: 0.82\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 Cheetah 相同逻辑：disease 不存在时 cure 无法展示 efficacy。Cartpole 中 trained dt_emb\n      未导致 CIVO，所以 dt_embed_dim=0 无额外保护效果。两组 eval 完全重叠 (670 vs 680, p=0.85)。\n      Causal narrative \"dt_embed → CIVO → collapse\" 在 Cartpole 中 vacuously true but uninformative。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole causal control\"\n        columns: [config, mean_eval_105K, mean_nve_peak, vs_baseline]\n        rows:\n          - [\"trained dt_emb (051)\", 680, 0.98, \"-10%\"]\n          - [\"dt_embed_dim=0 (052)\", 670, 0.82, \"-11%\"]\n          - [\"difference\", \"-10 (n.s.)\", \"-0.16\", \"~0%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole 051 vs 052: completely overlapping trajectories\"\n    analysis: >\n      Causal control 在 Cartpole 中 uninformative。两组行为一致，不提供 CIVO mechanism 的任何证据。\n\n  - name: \"NVE threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_034\"\n    description: \"Compute classification accuracy at multiple nve thresholds across all data\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_only_auroc: 1.0\n      walker_only_1.5x_accuracy: \"4/4 (100%)\"\n      cross_env_1.5x_accuracy: \"4/10 (40%)\"\n      cross_env_auroc: 0.58\n      optimal_threshold_cross_env: \"N/A (no threshold separates)\"\n      walker_1.3x_accuracy: \"4/4 (100%)\"\n      walker_1.7x_accuracy: \"3/4 (75%)\"\n      cheetah_1.3x_accuracy: \"0/6 (0% — no positives)\"\n      cartpole_1.3x_accuracy: \"0/6 (0% — no positives)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档指定 cross_env_nve_threshold_accuracy=[0.4,0.6]。分析逻辑：\n      Walker 内：trained dt_emb 4 seeds 全部 exceed 1.5x (true positives=4)，untrained 4 seeds 全部 <1.5x\n      (true negatives=4) → Walker AUROC=1.0，accuracy=100%。\n      加入 Cheetah+Cartpole：trained dt_emb 6 seeds 全部 <1.5x（都是 false negatives if we expect CIVO）。\n      Cross-env accuracy：如果将\"trained dt_emb 应该触发 nve>1.5x\"作为 hypothesis，则\n      true positives=4 (Walker), false negatives=6 (Cheetah+Cartpole), true negatives=10 (all untrained)\n      → sensitivity=4/10=40%, specificity=10/10=100%。Overall accuracy ≈ (4+10)/20 = 70%。\n      但 \"threshold as diagnostic\" 的 cross-env sensitivity 仅 40% → 作为通用 diagnostic 失败。\n      AUROC drop from 1.0 (Walker-only) to 0.58 (cross-env) 因为 Cheetah+Cartpole 的 trained dt_emb\n      scores 落在 0.8-1.3 range，与 untrained 的 0.7-1.0 range 大量重叠。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"NVE threshold cross-env analysis\"\n        columns: [threshold, walker_acc, cheetah_acc, cartpole_acc, overall_sensitivity, overall_specificity]\n        rows:\n          - [1.3, \"4/4\", \"1/3 FP?→ 0/3\", \"0/3\", \"4/10 (40%)\", \"10/10\"]\n          - [1.5, \"4/4\", \"0/3\", \"0/3\", \"4/10 (40%)\", \"10/10\"]\n          - [1.7, \"3/4\", \"0/3\", \"0/3\", \"3/10 (30%)\", \"10/10\"]\n          - [2.0, \"2/4\", \"0/3\", \"0/3\", \"2/10 (20%)\", \"10/10\"]\n      - name: \"AUROC by scope\"\n        columns: [scope, auroc, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker only\", 1.0, \"perfect separation\"]\n          - [\"Walker + Cheetah\", 0.67, \"degraded\"]\n          - [\"All 3 envs\", 0.58, \"near-random for cross-env generalization\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ROC curves: Walker-only (perfect) vs cross-env (near-diagonal)\"\n      - \"NVE distribution violin plots by env × dt_emb_condition\"\n    analysis: >\n      NVE>1.5x 作为通用 CIVO diagnostic 在 cross-env 下失效。它是 Walker-specific marker，不是\n      architectural vulnerability marker。论文必须将 claims 限制为 \"in Walker Walk\" 或引入 environment\n      characterization (reward nonlinearity, obs dimensionality) 作为 applicability conditions。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=2 imag + H=8\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"Diagnostic: is dt_emb TRAINING necessary for CIVO?\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_105K: 204\n      nve_peak: 0.47\n      nve_stable_range: [0.39, 0.47]\n      collapse: false\n      actor_loss_105K: 0.000179\n      mechanism: \"gradient starvation from frozen dt_emb\"\n      gate_dt_mean: 2.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有 exp_015b_frozen_dt_emb 数据完全匹配。Frozen dt_emb 阻止 CIVO（nve<0.5x, 远低于 1.5x threshold），\n      但代价是 gradient starvation：actor_loss→0，policy 无法从 frozen-embedding-conditioned critic\n      获得有效学习信号。Eval 停滞在 ~200（远低于 baseline 950 和 trained dt_emb 的初始 performance）。\n      在 worst 档下这被解释为：frozen dt_emb 不是 viable mitigation（too costly），且该结果仅在 Walker 中\n      observeable——在 Cheetah/Cartpole 中 frozen 与 trained 的差异更小因为 dt_emb 本身 less impactful。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"015 frozen dt_emb result\"\n        columns: [metric, value, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [\"eval_105K\", 204, \"22% baseline (severe degradation)\"]\n          - [\"nve_peak\", 0.47, \"far below 1.5x (no CIVO)\"]\n          - [\"actor_loss\", \"→0\", \"gradient starvation\"]\n          - [\"collapse\", \"no\", \"stable but low-performing\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"015 vs 008d vs baseline: frozen avoids CIVO but at extreme performance cost\"\n    analysis: >\n      Confirms dt_emb TRAINING is necessary for CIVO in Walker。但 worst 档论点：\n      这只在 Walker 中 informative，因为其他 envs 即使 TRAINED dt_emb 也不触发 CIVO。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 additional seeds (seed 3-4)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"Narrow true collapse probability of 008e_v3\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed3_eval_105K: 780\n      seed3_collapse: false\n      seed3_nve_peak: 0.85\n      seed4_eval_105K: 190\n      seed4_collapse: true\n      seed4_nve_105K: 2.95\n      seed4_collapse_mechanism: \"mixed (Pathway A onset at 95K)\"\n      total_collapse_rate: \"2/4 (50%)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档指定 walker_additional_seeds_nve_separation=[0.75,1.0]，意味着 additional seeds 可能\n      显示分离度略降。2/4 collapse rate (50%) 与 008d 的 collapse rate 相同——dt=1 imagination\n      未提供任何保护。更糟的是，seed 4 的崩溃可能展示 mixed dynamics（既有 value overestimation\n      又有 eval-driven instability），模糊 Pathway A/B 的 clean distinction。这在 worst 档下\n      被解读为：Walker Walk 中 trained dt_emb 的 vulnerability 是 multi-modal 的，不可简单归因于\n      单一 CIVO mechanism。50% collapse rate 本身可能是 Walker 的 reward landscape property\n      （~50% 的 initial condition 导致 late-stage instability），与 dt_emb 的 interaction 可能是\n      coincidental 而非 causal。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008e_v3 full 4-seed summary\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_105K, collapse, nve_peak, pathway]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 870, \"no\", 0.80, \"healthy\"]\n          - [2, 137, \"yes\", 3.78, \"Pathway B (eval-driven)\"]\n          - [3, 780, \"no\", 0.85, \"healthy\"]\n          - [4, 190, \"yes\", 2.95, \"mixed A/B\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-seed 008e_v3 eval trajectories: bimodal outcome (healthy ~800 or collapse ~150-190)\"\n    analysis: >\n      50% collapse rate 与 008d 相同 → dt=1 imagination mitigation 完全无效。Worst 档下此结果\n      进一步削弱 paper 的 prescriptive value。且 seed 4 的 mixed mechanism 模糊了 clean causal story。\n\n  - name: \"Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_060\"\n    description: \"Truncate imagination when RSSM prediction uncertainty exceeds threshold\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_105K: 520\n      vs_baseline: \"-45%\"\n      nve_peak: 1.35\n      collapse: false\n      truncation_rate_at_dt2: 0.65\n      effective_horizon: 5.2\n      vs_008d_improvement: \"+55% (520 vs 82.7@55K)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Uncertainty-gating 在 Walker 中部分有效（避免 collapse），但大幅截断 imagination（65% of dt=2\n      rollouts 被 truncate），导致 effective horizon 仅 5.2 steps（vs planned 15）。Eval 在 baseline\n      的 55% 水平——比 collapse 好但远低于 baseline。在 worst 档下这被解释为：(1) mitigation 在 Walker\n      中 works 但 cost 高（45% eval loss from truncation）；(2) 这种 mitigation 在 Cheetah/Cartpole 中\n      无意义因为不需要 truncation（CIVO 不存在）；(3) 无法判断 improvement 是来自 uncertainty-gating 本身\n      还是仅仅是因为 truncation 导致 shorter effective dt（approaching dt=1 naturally）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Uncertainty-gated pilot results\"\n        columns: [metric, value, vs_baseline, vs_008d]\n        rows:\n          - [\"eval_105K\", 520, \"-45%\", \"+528%\"]\n          - [\"nve_peak\", 1.35, \"N/A\", \"-35%\"]\n          - [\"truncation_rate\", \"65%\", \"N/A\", \"N/A\"]\n          - [\"effective_horizon\", 5.2, \"-65% of H=15\", \"N/A\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Uncertainty-gated eval trajectory with truncation rate overlay\"\n    analysis: >\n      Partial success in Walker but the improvement is likely explained by de facto horizon reduction\n      (5.2 ≈ H=5 → less exposure to dt>1 errors)。Not a principled solution; cross-env 无意义。\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: \"Third DMC environment for generalization — worst tier predicts no CIVO\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_mean_eval: 250\n      trained_dtEmb_mean_eval: 210\n      trained_dtEmb_nve_peak: 1.05\n      trained_dtEmb_vs_baseline: \"-16%\"\n      no_dtEmb_mean_eval: 205\n      collapse_count: \"0/3\"\n      nve_above_1.5x: \"0/3\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Hopper Hop 在 DreamerV3 中本身表现中等 (baseline ~200-300)。Worst 档预测与 Cheetah/Cartpole\n      一致：trained dt_emb 不触发 CIVO (nve<1.3x)，degradation 仅 16%（subsample 效应），\n      与 no_dtEmb 不可区分。进一步确认 CIVO 是 Walker-specific artifact。\n      Hopper 的 reward landscape 涉及 hop height + forward progress，虽然 nonlinear 但 Hopper\n      的 low baseline performance (250) 意味着 value estimates 的 absolute magnitude 小，\n      即使有 overestimation 也不足以形成正反馈（critic 的 absolute error 太小 to dominate actor gradient）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Hopper Hop summary (worst tier)\"\n        columns: [config, mean_eval_300K, nve_peak, collapse_rate]\n        rows:\n          - [\"baseline\", 250, \"N/A (reference)\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"trained dt_emb + sub ON\", 210, 1.05, \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"no dt_emb + sub ON\", 205, 0.80, \"0/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-environment summary: only Walker shows CIVO — environment-specific artifact\"\n    analysis: >\n      Fourth environment confirming CIVO non-replication。At this point the evidence is overwhelming：\n      Walker Walk 是 CIVO 能被观察到的唯一环境。论文必须 reframe 为 \"boundary conditions\" paper。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run exp_018 (Full-SGS) extrapolation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030 (related)\"\n    description: \"Full stop-gradient on obs decoders → dt_emb 仅保留 7% KL gradient\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_full_sgs_eval_105K: 160\n      walker_full_sgs_nve_peak: 0.55\n      walker_full_sgs_collapse: false\n      walker_full_sgs_actor_loss: \"→0 (gradient starvation)\"\n      mechanism: \"obs decoder detach kills 93% of dt_emb gradient → effectively frozen\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Full-SGS 移除 93% of dt_emb gradient (obs decoders)，仅保留 7% KL dynamics gradient。\n      效果类似 frozen dt_emb (plan_015)：CIVO 被 eliminate 但 performance 严重退化，因为\n      dt_emb 几乎不训练 → 与 015b 的 gradient starvation 相似。在 worst 档下，Full-SGS 是\n      另一个 \"过度干预\" 方案：解决了 CIVO 但 payoff 为负（eval 远低于 baseline）。\n      且此干预仅在 Walker 中 relevant——其他环境没有 CIVO 需要 prevent。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"SGS variants comparison (Walker)\"\n        columns: [config, eval_105K, nve_peak, collapse, mechanism]\n        rows:\n          - [\"016e (reward SGS only)\", \"31.7@95K\", 10.42, \"yes\", \"no-op (reward grad=0)\"]\n          - [\"018 (Full-SGS: obs detach)\", 160, 0.55, \"no\", \"gradient starvation\"]\n          - [\"015b (frozen dt_emb)\", 204, 0.47, \"no\", \"gradient starvation\"]\n          - [\"008d (no intervention)\", \"82.7@55K\", 4.12, \"yes\", \"classic CIVO\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"SGS intervention spectrum: from no-op (016e) to over-kill (018/015b)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Full-SGS and frozen dt_emb produce similar outcomes: CIVO prevented but performance destroyed.\n      No middle ground found. In worst tier this is: \"the only interventions that prevent CIVO in Walker\n      also destroy learning — suggesting the trained dt_emb is load-bearing for what learning does occur.\"\n\n  - name: \"Cross-environment NVE threshold diagnostic validation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_034\"\n    description: \"Formal statistical evaluation of nve>1.5x as universal CIVO diagnostic\"\n    expected_results:\n      classification_matrix:\n        walker_TP: 4\n        walker_FN: 0\n        walker_TN: 4\n        walker_FP: 0\n        cheetah_TP: 0\n        cheetah_FN: 3\n        cheetah_TN: 3\n        cheetah_FP: 0\n        cartpole_TP: 0\n        cartpole_FN: 3\n        cartpole_TN: 3\n        cartpole_FP: 0\n      overall_sensitivity: 0.40\n      overall_specificity: 1.0\n      overall_accuracy: 0.70\n      cross_env_auroc: 0.58\n      conclusion: \"Threshold is Walker-specific; fails as universal diagnostic\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cross-env 分析的核心问题：threshold 的 specificity 完美 (1.0) 因为 untrained dt_emb 从不\n      exceed 1.5x（在所有环境中一致）。但 sensitivity 仅 40% 因为 Cheetah+Cartpole 的 trained dt_emb\n      也不 exceed 1.5x。如果我们将 \"trained dt_emb\" 定义为 \"should trigger CIVO\"，那么 6/10 trained\n      cases 是 false negatives。AUROC 0.58 接近 random (0.5)。这证明 nve>1.5x 不是 architectural\n      vulnerability marker，而是 Walker-Walk-specific pathology marker。Diagnostic 的适用范围\n      必须被 explicitly bounded。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-env diagnostic evaluation\"\n        columns: [metric, walker_only, all_envs, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Sensitivity\", \"1.0 (4/4)\", \"0.40 (4/10)\", \"fails cross-env\"]\n          - [\"Specificity\", \"1.0 (4/4)\", \"1.0 (10/10)\", \"high (vacuously)\"]\n          - [\"AUROC\", 1.0, 0.58, \"near-random cross-env\"]\n          - [\"PPV\", \"1.0\", \"1.0\", \"if positive, always correct\"]\n          - [\"NPV\", \"1.0\", \"0.63\", \"if negative, 37% chance missed CIVO\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ROC curve overlay: Walker-only (AUC=1.0) vs all-envs (AUC=0.58)\"\n    analysis: >\n      NVE>1.5x 作为 universal diagnostic 的 cross-env validity 被 falsified。\n      论文必须将其定位为 \"environment-conditional diagnostic\" 并提供 applicability criteria\n      (reward nonlinearity > X, obs_dim > Y, reward_gap > 2.0x)。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb) seeds 1-2 — boundary condition\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Additional context for worst-tier reframing\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 680\n      seed1_nve_range: [0.55, 0.80]\n      seed2_eval_105K: 550\n      seed2_nve_range: [0.60, 0.85]\n      cross_seed_eval_cv: 0.15\n      interpretation: \"Value suppression consistent but eval benefit variable\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 worst 档的 reframing 中，008a 的 additional seeds 显示 value suppression 在 Walker 内\n      robust (all nve<1.0x) 但 eval 表现 variable (550-778, CV=15%)。这削弱了 \"untrained dt_emb =\n      practical solution\" 的叙事——protection 有效但 performance 代价 unpredictable (15-40% below baseline)。\n      Worst 档将此解释为：即使在 Walker Walk 这个 CIVO 最强的环境中，mitigation 的 benefit/cost tradeoff\n      也是 uncertain。在不存在 CIVO 的其他环境中，untrained dt_emb 纯粹是 unnecessary overhead。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008a multi-seed (Walker only, worst tier context)\"\n        columns: [seed, eval_105K, nve_range, vs_baseline, trend]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 778, \"0.59-0.93\", \"-15%\", \"zigzag recovery, best case\"]\n          - [1, 680, \"0.55-0.80\", \"-26%\", \"moderate recovery\"]\n          - [2, 550, \"0.60-0.85\", \"-40%\", \"slow, still below 75K peak\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"008a 3-seed with IQM: large CI band undermines 'near-baseline' claim\"\n    analysis: >\n      IQM across 3 seeds: ~670 (-27% baseline)。原 seed 0 的 778 是上界 outlier。\n      Worst 档利用此修正 C3 claim 的强度从 \"85% baseline\" 到 \"60-85% baseline (IQM ~73%)\"。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"804c4c93-33c8-4f5e-98da-2ef3